<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39964" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quālĭbet</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-lŭbet</span></b> , abl. from
		quilibet), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>where it
				pleases</i>, i. e. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Where you will</i>, <i>everywhere</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qualibet perambula aedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 3, 2, 122</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Aul. 4, 4, 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quisquis amore tenetur, eat tutusque sacerque
					qualibet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					1, 2, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transitum praebent (flumina),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 13, 13</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>As you please</i>, <i>anyhow</i>, <i>in any way</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qualubet esse notus optas?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					40, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">76,
		13</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
